    "user_request_original": "Design a symmetric Fabry-Perot narrowband bandpass filter for 1550 nm LiDAR reception. Incident medium is air. Substrate is Fused Silica. Use only Ta2O5 (Gao) (high index) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) (low index) materials. Stack topology: Air | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao)(cavity) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Fused Silica. This is 11 layers total (5 pairs on each side plus one cavity layer). Optimize all individual layer thicknesses in nanometers. Target wavelength is 1550 nm at normal incidence. Maximize transmittance at 1550 nm with soft target ≥0.95. Minimize transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Total layers must not exceed 30.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thicknesses of all 21 finite Ta2O5/SiO2 layers in a symmetric Fabry-Perot stack for 1550 nm normal incidence. Maximize transmittance at 1550 nm (target ≥0.95) while minimizing transmittance across 1400–1500 nm and 1600–1700 nm stopbands. Total coating layers remain fixed at 21, within the ≤30 limit. Resolve materials via local registry and report results post-optimization.",
